WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.740
Stuart Varney: Socialism
leads to decline and ruin.

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:06.332
Bernie Sanders: They may
hate democratic socialism.

00:00:06.332 --> 00:00:08.098
Sean Hannity: And they
think we, the people,

00:00:08.098 --> 00:00:10.310
are stupid, helpless, uneducated.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:15.165
Sanders: But they absolutely
love corporate socialism.

00:00:15.165 --> 00:00:19.265
Donald Trump: We will never
be a socialist country.

00:00:19.265 --> 00:00:20.950
(audience applauds and cheers)

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:22.341
Manny Fidel: The back-and-forth between

00:00:22.341 --> 00:00:24.990
Republicans and Democrats on socialism

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:27.020
is enough to give you whiplash.

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:28.753
But one thing is true:

00:00:28.753 --> 00:00:30.840
socialism is on the rise.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.240
Forty-three percent of Americans now say

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:36.574
that some form of socialism
is good for the country,

00:00:36.574 --> 00:00:40.150
compared to just 25% in 1942.

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:43.940
Comrades are popping up like
Starbucks all over America.

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:45.600
As much as Republicans hate this,

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:48.010
it turns out they have
themselves to thank.

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:49.540
It is their own policies

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:52.510
and actions that have
positioned democratic socialism

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:54.800
as a legitimate option for Americans.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:57.680
Congratulations; you've played yourself.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:58.840
Here's the trend.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.270
Republicans dismantle
moderate liberal policies.

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:04.700
They attack those policies as socialism

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:07.540
and institute their own far-right ideas.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:09.463
That causes Democrats to respond

00:01:09.463 --> 00:01:12.160
with an even more left-leaning proposal.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:14.060
And because of that back-and-forth,

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:16.080
more Americans are now considering

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:19.230
giving some form of socialism a chance.

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:22.330
Herman Cain: The C in capitalism
stands for competition.

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:25.920
The S in socialism
stands for state control.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.480
Fidel: The S here actually
stands for straw man,

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:31.530
because the type of socialism
that Republicans are attacking

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:33.341
isn't quite the same as the one that

00:01:33.341 --> 00:01:35.040
progressives are pushing for.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:38.070
Traditional socialism pushes
for collective ownership

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:39.830
of all means of production,

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:42.235
either through direct ownership by workers

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:43.460
or the government.

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:45.580
Democratic socialism is the idea

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:46.960
that the government should provide

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:49.650
just the basic needs for its citizens,

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:52.330
like healthcare, education, and more.

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:54.620
This is the type of
socialism being promoted

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:57.040
by politicians like Sen. Bernie Sanders

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:00.130
and Rep. Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez.

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:02.700
Now, Republicans love
to scream "socialism"

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:05.200
at any policy that
involves the government.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.160
They'd probably call their kids socialists

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:08.790
if they asked for an allowance.

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:12.010
But remember, it's Republican
policy that contributed

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:15.220
to the rise of Democratic
socialism in the first place.

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:17.800
Obamacare is the perfect example.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:21.710
It was passed in 2010, and
literally minutes later,

00:02:21.710 --> 00:02:23.769
a group of Republicans filed a lawsuit

00:02:23.769 --> 00:02:25.260
against it, saying it was

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.080
Because Obamacare mandated

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:34.155
that people sign up for
healthcare or pay a fee,

00:02:34.155 --> 00:02:37.180
Republicans started calling
it a government takeover,

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:39.115
likening it to socialism.

00:02:39.115 --> 00:02:40.767
Mike Pence: And the
American people don't want

00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:43.330
a government takeover of healthcare.

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:45.700
Fidel: They immediately
obstructed enrollment efforts

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:48.600
by passing laws intended
to limit and defund

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.141
Obamacare outreach.

00:02:50.141 --> 00:02:52.450
Fourteen red states eventually dropped out

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:54.790
of Obamacare's Medicaid expansion,

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:58.840
leaving an estimated 3.6
million people uninsured.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:03.000
In 2017, Republicans wanted
to repeal Obamacare's rule

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.970
that people have to sign up
for healthcare or pay a fee.

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:07.410
The Congressional Budget Office

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:09.820
predicted that if they
succeeded in doing this,

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:11.710
many people would lose healthcare

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:14.670
and the amount people pay
per month would go up.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:16.900
Republicans repealed the rule anyways,

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:19.540
and, of course, that
helps keep premiums high.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:22.240
People started getting
tired of the current system.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:26.640
In 2018, 79% of Americans
were dissatisfied

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:28.650
with the total cost of healthcare.

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:29.930
They're looking for relief,

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:33.220
and the most ambitious and
appealing alternative is:

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:34.120
Kirsten Gillibrand: Medicare for All.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:35.190
Michael Bennet: Medicare for All.

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:36.650
Sanders: Medicare for All.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:38.870
Fidel: "Medicare for All"
is a proposal that says

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:40.740
the government should
be providing Medicare

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:43.340
not just for those over 65 years old,

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:44.431
but for everyone.

00:03:44.431 --> 00:03:46.350
In fact, even moderate Democrats

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:48.770
are pushing for what's
called the "public option,"

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:51.750
a proposal for a government-run
healthcare alternative

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:54.100
that would compete with private insurers.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.640
But even modest reforms
like the public option

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.570
are being blasted as
"socialist" by Republicans.

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:01.090
Meridian Paulton: You know,
the public option is just

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:04.490
a Trojan horse for government-run
healthcare across the map,

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:05.940
for socialist healthcare.

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:07.200
Fidel: Because Republicans have been

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.710
calling everything socialism forever,

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:12.380
Americans found themselves
defining socialism

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:14.950
as something different
than the traditional form.

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:18.320
Since 1949, fewer people think socialism

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:19.990
is about government control

00:04:19.990 --> 00:04:22.910
and more people think
socialism is about equality,

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:25.990
benefits, services, and Medicare for All.

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:28.920
Even though Republicans
contributed to the situation

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:31.940
that made Medicare for
All a legitimate proposal,

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:34.380
you can probably guess
how they feel about it.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:36.780
Katrina Pierson: I think we're
past insanity at this point.

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:38.260
Charlie Kirk: It is so beyond realistic,

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:41.140
it's almost not even worthy
of even analyzing the policy.

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:43.223
Jesse Watters: Now, let's look
at the facts about socialism,

00:04:43.223 --> 00:04:44.273
shall we?

00:04:44.273 --> 00:04:48.720
Venezuela. Sick people
are taking dog medicine.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:50.400
Fidel: Another example of Republicans

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:53.008
contributing to socialism's popularity:

00:04:53.008 --> 00:04:54.758
the Green New Deal.

00:04:54.758 --> 00:04:57.300
In the years leading up to
the Trump administration,

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:58.980
progressive efforts for the environment

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:00.980
were looking relatively good.

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:02.850
Activists were halting the construction

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:05.310
of harmful pipelines across America,

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:07.830
the world became more
aware of climate change,

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:11.160
and the Obama administration
opted into the Paris accord,

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:12.618
a legally binding agreement

00:05:14.968 --> 00:05:17.418
that aims to limit global warming.

00:05:17.418 --> 00:05:19.860
However, when Trump became president,

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:23.080
the country did a one-eighty
on environmental policy.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:24.790
Trump signed orders that advanced

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:27.250
the Keystone and Dakota Access pipelines

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:30.076
that Native Americans said
threatened water resources

00:05:30.076 --> 00:05:31.583
and sacred sites.

00:05:31.583 --> 00:05:34.079
Republicans passed the
resolution allowing for

00:05:34.079 --> 00:05:36.350
mining waste to be dumped in streams.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:39.300
Trump appointed Scott
Pruitt, of all people,

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:41.940
to lead the Environmental
Protection Agency.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:44.040
Pruitt repeatedly sued the EPA

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:45.960
while he was Oklahoma's attorney general,

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:47.970
and when Pruitt resigned from the post,

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:51.010
Trump replaced him with
a former coal lobbyist.

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:54.480
Sanders: Scientific community
has said that climate change

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:57.780
is one of the great
crises facing our planet.

00:05:57.780 --> 00:05:59.547
Andrew Wheeler: I would not
call it the greatest crisis,

00:05:59.547 --> 00:06:00.380
no sir.

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:01.670
Fidel: In June 2017,

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:04.680
Trump pulled out of the Paris
accord I mentioned earlier.

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:06.140
I think you get the point.

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:07.730
This made it clear to progressives

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:09.750
that Republican views on climate change

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:12.020
were detrimental to the environment.

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:14.145
Then, in February 2019,

00:06:14.145 --> 00:06:16.628
AOC introduced the Green New Deal,

00:06:16.628 --> 00:06:19.590
a massively ambitious
plan to curb bad emissions

00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:22.110
and create jobs in
clean energy industries.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:24.380
It's a response to the
Trump administration's

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:26.710
callous actions towards the environment,

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:28.540
and it's pretty popular.

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:30.523
Sixty-three percent of adults believe that

00:06:30.523 --> 00:06:32.714
the Green New Deal is a good idea,

00:06:32.714 --> 00:06:35.732
and 83% of Democrats agree.

00:06:35.732 --> 00:06:39.360
So, once again, even though
Republicans contributed

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:42.240
to the situation that
led to this proposal,

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:44.090
you can guess how they feel about it.

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:45.250
Steve Hilton: It's really extreme.

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:46.580
They are actually talking about

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:48.540
controlling the entire economy.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:51.710
Sara Carter: It requires
people to turn on each other

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:54.920
and for a government to
answer for everything.

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:56.780
Fidel: These attacks aren't new, either.

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:58.370
Let's go back in time a bit.

00:06:58.370 --> 00:06:59.750
During the Great Depression,

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:02.130
FDR was working to pass the New Deal,

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:03.760
a series of public programs

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:06.340
created to provide financial
aid to the country.

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:07.770
But wealthy businessmen,

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:09.810
aka people who didn't want the government

00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:11.680
to play a larger role in their lives,

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:14.330
opposed the deal and formed a new party.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:17.460
The American Liberty League
was so against the New Deal

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:20.744
that they compared it to
policies from the Soviet Union.

00:07:32.416 --> 00:07:33.249
(clears throat)

00:07:33.249 --> 00:07:34.707
In the following decades,

00:07:34.707 --> 00:07:37.700
this tactic went on to
become a Republican favorite.

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:39.780
Sebastian Gorka: You
are on the front lines

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:43.930
of the war against communism
coming back to America

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:47.170
under the guise of democratic socialism.

00:07:47.170 --> 00:07:48.260
Frank Luntz: If you're a young person

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:50.170
and you tell someone of the opposite sex

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:51.300
that you're a socialist,

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:53.140
you're much more likely to get some action

00:07:53.140 --> 00:07:54.284
at the end of the evening.

00:07:54.284 --> 00:07:56.980
(laughs)

00:07:56.980 --> 00:07:59.070
Fidel: Before I go
update my Tinder profile,

00:07:59.070 --> 00:08:00.370
I'll give you one more reason

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:02.760
why socialism is on the rise in America.

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:05.280
It's simply because, politically speaking,

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:08.640
Trump's policies have brought
us so far to the right,

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:11.210
it only makes sense that
new opposition to Trump

00:08:11.210 --> 00:08:13.340
would come from the far left.

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:15.350
This is how two democratic socialists

00:08:15.350 --> 00:08:17.660
were elected to Congress in 2018,

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:20.420
and it might be what gives
Bernie Sanders more steam

00:08:20.420 --> 00:08:22.070
heading into the election.

00:08:22.070 --> 00:08:25.530
Today's political issues
are complicated and nuanced.

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:27.990
If the Republicans'
solutions to those issues

00:08:27.990 --> 00:08:30.890
only benefit those at the
top, you can't blame voters

00:08:30.890 --> 00:08:33.173
for looking for more radical alternatives.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:36.770
Godless union of the Soviet.

00:08:36.770 --> 00:08:40.263
I accidentally sounded like
Bernie Sanders there. (laughs)

